{"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"],"generated":true}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry is a list someone has to keep in step with the code: every analytics event type in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, every route in a table, every dependency registered in one function at startup. A new type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that isn’t added works everywhere except where the list is read, and nothing tells you. Moving the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list onto LinkerSets takes four steps, and the list is deleted at the end."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Take an analytics library whose events are types conforming to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsEvent"},{"type":"text","text":", collected by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hand so the library can validate their schemas at launch:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol AnalyticsEvent {","    static var name: String { get }","}","","\/\/ Every module's events, listed by hand.","let allEvents: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] = [","    Login.self,","    Logout.self,","    PurchaseCompleted.self,","]"]},{"text":"1. Give the library a macro","anchor":"1-Give-the-library-a-macro","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick a kind (“evnt” is "},{"code":"0x6576_6E74","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" explains) and add a compiler plugin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose macro requires the protocol, so its records hold "},{"code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Analytics.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The library declares the macro and the kind, re-exports LinkerSets for the expansion, and reads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the set for its users:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let events = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x6576_6E74)  \/\/ \"evnt\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"AnalyticsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")","","public enum AnalyticsEvents {","    public static var all: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] {","        LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The re-export is required. The expansion lands in each user’s file and calls LinkerSets’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord"},{"text":" there, so that file must see the LinkerSets module. A library that imports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSets without re-exporting it leaves its users’ files failing with “no macro named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"‘linkerSetRecord’” unless each one imports LinkerSets too. The re-export also puts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" in scope wherever the library is imported. Keep the kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"internal and hand users the values through the library’s own API (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsEvents.all"},{"text":"), so the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set is read in one place.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation has the package targets this needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"2. Read the set beside the list","anchor":"2-Read-the-set-beside-the-list","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Before touching any event, read both and compare them, in a test or a debug build:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let discovered = AnalyticsEvents.all","let missing = allEvents.filter { listed in !discovered.contains { $0 == listed } }"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"type":"text","text":" starts as the whole list and shrinks as events are marked."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"3. Mark each event where it’s declared","anchor":"3-Mark-each-event-where-its-declared","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@Event","struct Login: AnalyticsEvent {","    static let name = \"login\"","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that doesn’t conform fails to compile. A generic event type, or one nested in a generic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type, is refused with a message, as "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse"},{"type":"text","text":" lists; such a type needs its concrete"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specializations listed by hand, or a concrete wrapper."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"4. Delete the list","anchor":"4-Delete-the-list","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once "},{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty, the library reads the set instead:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let allEvents = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and the hand-written array goes. A new event is registered by writing ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on it, in whichever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module declares it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Other registries","anchor":"Other-registries","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The same steps fit any list whose entries can be declared as constants, functions or types:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Routes"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route static let profile = Route(path: \"\/profile\")"},{"type":"text","text":", read as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<Route>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Migrations"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"@Migration static func addUsers(_ db: inout Database)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", read as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"LinkerSet<(inout Database) -> Void>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", sorted by a version the migration declares."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dependency registrations"}]},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Registration static func register(_ container: Container)"},{"text":", each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module registering its own factories, read and called once at startup.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry whose order matters gets it from the entries, never from the set: the linker’s order is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stable but not one you choose ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"title":"Platforms and linking"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","title":"Declaring a kind","abstract":[{"text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}],"title":"LinkerSets"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSetKind":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind","title":"LinkerSetKind","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tag that says which client a linker-set record belongs to."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSetKind","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkersetkind","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetKind","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","abstract":[{"text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"What the macros refuse"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSet":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"produce.","type":"text"}],"title":"LinkerSet","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkerset","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","abstract":[{"text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Finding records"}}}